use std
into impostor_check.amni

Imports: os, math, gfx, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.shapes and gfx.scene3d. A standalone GPU program that checks impostors for far instanced trees against the real meshes (bars I1 to I5 of hc/lib/gfx/README.md), prints one line per bar, then "impostor: ok", "impostor: FAILED", or "impostor: skipped" when no GPU opens. When the program gets an argument it is a folder, and the comparison pictures are saved there as PNG files. These already exist; never define them here: `gfx::open_headless(w, h) bool`, `s3d::init(w, h)`, `s3d::atmosphere(to_sun float3, power, haze, clouds)`, `shapes::material(rgb float3, metallic f32, roughness f32) gltf::Material` (fields `double_sided` bool, `shading` int, `shade_a` and `shade_b` float4), `shapes::vertex(p float3, n float3, u f32, v f32, t float4)` (appends one vertex to `gltf::verts`), `shapes::finish_groups(vfirst int, ifirst int, lo float3, hi float3, materials, counts) int` (materials and counts are array literals; returns an asset), `shapes::plane(half f32, m) int`, `gltf::verts` (f32, `gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS` floats per vertex, position at `gltf::AT_POS`, vertex color at `gltf::AT_COL`, four floats), `gltf::indices` (a growable u32 array of indices relative to the asset's first vertex), `s3d::add(asset) int`, `s3d::items[item].visible` bool, `s3d::place(item, matrix)`, `s3d::add_instances(asset, matrices) int` (a growable array of `gfx::mat4`; returns a set), `s3d::instances[set]` with fields `visible` bool, `shadow` bool, `imp` int (minus 1 for none), `imp_distance` f32 and `imp_band` f32, `s3d::impostor(asset) int` (bakes an impostor and returns its handle), `s3d::imps[handle].tier` int, `s3d::instance_triangles(set) int`, `s3d::sun` (fields `shadows` bool and `shadow_far` f32), `s3d::view` (an `s3d::Camera { eye, target, up, fov_y (f32), near, far }`), `s3d::nd` (the normals pass target: RGBA half floats, 8 bytes a pixel, view depth in the fourth channel), `s3d::render(target)`, `gfx::flush()`, `gfx::render_target(w, h, gfx::RGBA8)`, `gfx::read_pixels(texture)` giving bytes, `gfx::save_png(texture, path) bool`, `gfx::translate(float3)`, `gfx::rotate(axis float3, angle f32)`, `gfx::scale(float3)`, `gfx::mul(a, b)` for two matrices, `gfx::mat4_identity`, `os::clock() real` (seconds), `os::args()` (the first entry is the program).

Module constants: `W = 1280`, `H = 720`, `PI real = 3.141592653589793`. Module vars: `seed` u32 starting at 2463534242, `outdir` a byte string, empty at start.

`rnd() f32` steps an xorshift32 generator on `seed`: xor seed with itself shifted left by 13, then with itself shifted right by 17, then with itself shifted left by 5; return seed as real divided by 4294967296.0, as f32.

`v3(x real, y real, z real) float3` builds a float3 from three reals.

`cyl(vfirst int, a float3, b float3, ra f32, rb f32, sides int)` appends a tapered open tube from a (radius ra) to b (radius rb). Let ax be linalg's unit3 of b minus a; helper is (1, 0, 0) when the absolute value of ax's y is below 0.9, else (0, 0, 1); p is unit3 of cross3 of ax and helper; q is cross3 of ax and p. Let base be the vertex count (`gltf::verts` length over `gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS`) minus vfirst. For i from 0 to sides inclusive, with angle t equal to i over sides times two pi, the outward direction o is p times cosine of t plus q times sine of t; append with `shapes::vertex` the bottom vertex a plus o times ra and then the top vertex b plus o times rb, both with normal o, u i over sides, v 0 for bottom and 1 for top, tangent (ax, 1). Then for each i below sides, with bottom index k equal to base plus twice i, push to `gltf::indices` as u32 the triangles k, k plus 2, k plus 3 and k, k plus 3, k plus 1.

`tree() int` builds the test tree as one asset with two primitives. Set `seed` to 2463534242. vfirst is the current vertex count and ifirst the current index count. The trunk is `cyl` from (0, 0, 0) to (0, 6, 0) with radii 0.28 and 0.12 and 12 sides. Then 9 branches: for k from 0 to 8, y is 2.6 plus 0.4 times k, angle a is k times 2.4, direction is unit3 of (cosine of a, 0.55 plus 0.1 times `rnd`, sine of a), length is 2.2 plus 0.6 times `rnd`; `cyl` from (0, y, 0) to that point plus direction times length, radii 0.09 and 0.03, 6 sides. nb is the index count now minus ifirst. Then 2400 leaves. For each leaf: draw a direction on the unit sphere by picking three numbers, each 2 times `rnd` minus 1, until their length is between 0.05 and 1, then normalizing; f is 0.45 plus 0.55 times the cube root of `rnd`; the leaf center is (0, 6, 0) plus the direction scaled by f times (3.0, 3.5, 3.0) per axis; the face normal n is unit3 of the direction plus a random vector whose three parts are each 1.6 times `rnd` minus 0.8; s is unit3 of cross3 of n and (0.3, 1, 0.2); t is cross3 of n and s; with hw 0.11 and hl 0.15, the four corners in order are center minus t times hl, center plus s times hw, center plus t times hl, center minus s times hw; each gets `shapes::vertex` with normal n, uv (0.5, 0), (1, 0.5), (0.5, 1), (0, 0.5), tangent (s, 1). Then the leaf's color: k is 0.7 plus 0.6 times `rnd`, h is `rnd`; set the vertex color of the leaf's four vertices to k times (0.85 plus 0.3 times h), k, k times (0.9 minus 0.2 times h), and 1. Its indices relative to vfirst, with first corner index c, are c, c plus 1, c plus 2 and c, c plus 2, c plus 3. nl is the index count now minus ifirst minus nb. lo and hi are the smallest and largest x, y, z over every vertex from vfirst on. Bark is `shapes::material((0.25, 0.17, 0.11), 0, 0.9)`. Leaf is `shapes::material((0.16, 0.36, 0.09), 0, 0.7)` with `double_sided` true, `shading` 5, `shade_a` (0.8, 1.0, 0.4, 0.5) and `shade_b` (0.3, 0, 0, 0). Return `shapes::finish_groups(vfirst, ifirst, lo, hi, [bark, leaf], [nb, nl])`.

`shot(rt gfx::Texture)` returns a growable byte array: it renders to rt and flushes, two times, then returns a copy of `gfx::read_pixels(rt)`.

`aim(eye float3, target float3, up float3)` sets `s3d::view` to that eye, target and up with `fov_y` 0.9, near 0.1 and far 800.

`save(rt gfx::Texture, name)` (name a read-only byte string) does nothing when `outdir` is empty, else `gfx::save_png(rt, outdir + "/" + name + ".png")`.

`mask(a, b)` returns a growable byte array (a and b read-only byte slices of W by H RGBA8 pixels) returns one byte per pixel, 1 when the largest absolute difference among red, green and blue is above 7, else 0.

`count(m) int` (m a read-only byte slice) is the number of nonzero bytes.

`block_err(m1, m2) real` (two read-only masks) splits the image into 8 by 8 blocks; f1 and f2 are each block's share of set pixels; returns the sum of the absolute differences of f1 and f2 divided by the sum of the larger of f1 and f2, or 0 when that sum is 0.

`luma(px, i int) real` (px a read-only byte slice) is 0.2126 times the red byte plus 0.7152 times green plus 0.0722 times blue of pixel i.

`mean_luma(px, m1, m2) real` (all read-only byte slices) is the mean `luma` of px over the pixels set in m1 or m2; 0 when there are none.

`block_psnr(a, b, m1, m2) real` (all read-only byte slices) finds the bounding box of the pixels set in m1 or m2 (99 when there are none); for every 8 by 8 block of the image that overlaps that box it takes the mean of each of red, green and blue over the whole block in a and in b; mse is the mean of the squared differences of those means over all such blocks and channels; returns 99 when mse is below 1e-12, else 10 times log10 of 65025 divided by mse.

`within(x real, lo real, hi real) bool` is true when x is at least lo and at most hi.

`median(xs) real` (xs a growable real array) sorts a copy ascending and returns the middle element (the element at index count over 2), or 1e9 when empty.

`depths(px)` returns a growable real array (px a read-only byte slice of W by H pixels, 8 bytes each) returns the view depth of every pixel: the fourth half float of the pixel, decoded from its two little-endian bytes at offset 6 and 7 as an IEEE half float: sign from the top bit, 5 exponent bits, 10 fraction bits; exponent 0 gives fraction times 2 to the minus 24; exponent 31 gives 65504; else (1024 plus fraction) times 2 to the (exponent minus 25).

`main()`: open headless W by H (print "impostor: skipped" and stop when it fails). When `os::args()` has a second entry, `outdir` is it. `s3d::init(W, H)`; `s3d::temporal = 0`; `s3d::ssr_on = false`; `s3d::ssgi_on = false`; `s3d::gi_on = false`; `s3d::look.bloom = 0.0`; `s3d::sun.shadows = true`; `s3d::sun.shadow_far = 160.0`. el is 40 degrees in radians; `s3d::atmosphere` with to_sun (0.6 times cosine of el, sine of el, 0.8 times cosine of el), 3.5, 1.0, 0.3. rt is a W by H RGBA8 render target. asset is `tree()`; ground is `s3d::add(shapes::plane(400.0, shapes::material((0.35, 0.33, 0.3), 0, 0.9)))` placed at the identity, with `visible` false. one is `s3d::add_instances(asset, [gfx::mat4_identity])`. imp is `s3d::impostor(asset)`. center is (0, 4.8, 0). Helpers inside main: `shot_none()` sets the set's `visible` false and returns `shot(rt)`; `shot_mesh()` sets `visible` true and `imp` minus 1 and returns `shot(rt)`; `shot_imp()` sets `visible` true, `imp` to imp, `imp_distance` 0 and `imp_band` 0 and returns `shot(rt)`; these all act on set one.
I1 and I2 together: ok1 starts true; worst block error, lowest and highest count ratio, largest luminance error and lowest PSNR are tracked; dm and dc collect, per view, the median depth difference and the control median. For each distance d in 70 and 120, each height mode in 0 and 1, and each k from 0 to 6: heading th is 17 plus 360 times k over 7, in degrees, as radians. Mode 0: eye (d times sine of th, 1.7, d times cosine of th). Mode 1: eye is center plus d times (cosine of 25 degrees times sine of th, sine of 25 degrees, cosine of 25 degrees times cosine of th). `aim(eye, center, (0, 1, 0))`. Take p0 from `shot_none()`, pm from `shot_mesh()` and, when d is 70 and the mode is 0, keep nm, a copy of `gfx::read_pixels(s3d::nd)`; then pi from `shot_imp()`; for k 0 save rt as "i1_imp_" plus the distance and mode (like "i1_imp_70_0"), and before taking pi re-render the mesh view to save "i1_mesh_70_0" the same way (only when k is 0). For the I2 views keep ni from `s3d::nd` right after `shot_imp()`, then set `s3d::imps[imp].tier` to 5, take `shot(rt)` and keep nc from `s3d::nd`, and set the tier back to 1. mm is `mask(p0, pm)` and mi is `mask(p0, pi)`. The view passes when `block_err` is at most 0.2, the count ratio (count of mi over count of mm, 0 when mm is empty) is within 0.85 and 1.15, the luminance error (absolute of `mean_luma(pi)` over `mean_luma(pm)` minus 1, both over the union) is at most 0.1, and `block_psnr` is at least 25. Print "I1 view D M K: err E count C luma L psnr P" with " ok" or " FAIL" per view and fold into ok1. For the I2 views: from `depths` of nm, ni and nc, over the pixels set in both mm and mi, collect the absolute differences mesh minus impostor and mesh minus control; push their medians to dm and dc. Print "I1 picture: worst err E count LO..HI luma L psnr P" with " ok" or " FAIL". ok2 is true when every entry of dm is at most 0.5 and every entry of dc is above 1.0; print "I2 depth: median D control C" (the largest of dm and the smallest of dc) with " ok" or " FAIL".
I3: `s3d::atmosphere` with to_sun at 30 degrees up the same way; `s3d::sun.shadow_far = 220.0`; ground `visible` true; `aim((0, 150, 0.0001), (0, 0, 0), (0, 0, 1))`. q0 from `shot_none()`, qm from `shot_mesh()` (save "i3_mesh"), qi from `shot_imp()` (save "i3_imp"), then with the set's `shadow` false qc from `shot_imp()`, and `shadow` back to true. A pixel (x, y) is on the far ground when, with nx equal to (x plus 0.5) over W times 2 minus 1 and ny equal to 1 minus (y plus 0.5) over H times 2, gx is minus nx times the tangent of 0.45 times W over H times 150 and gz is ny times the tangent of 0.45 times 150, the length of (gx, gz) is above 4. Each shadow mask is the far-ground pixels whose `luma` is below 0.85 times the `luma` of q0 there. Pass when `block_err` of the impostor and mesh masks is at most 0.25, the impostor count over the mesh count is within 0.8 and 1.25, and the control count over the mesh count is below 0.1. Print "I3 shadow: err E count C control K" with " ok" or " FAIL". Set the ground `visible` false and the sun back to 40 degrees, `s3d::sun.shadow_far = 160.0`.
I4: set one's `visible` false. Set `seed` to 7. Build 2025 matrices: for i and j from 0 to 44, position (12 times i plus 6 times (2 times `rnd` minus 1) over 2, 0, 12 times j minus 264 plus 6 times (2 times `rnd` minus 1) over 2), turn 2 pi times `rnd`, scale 0.85 plus 0.3 times `rnd`: translate times rotate about y times uniform scale. forest is `s3d::add_instances(asset, those)`. Ground `visible` true. `aim((-8, 1.7, 0), (100, 1.7, 0), (0, 1, 0))`. A run sets the forest's `imp` (minus 1 for meshes, or imp with `imp_distance` 50 and `imp_band` 14), renders 140 warm-up frames (render to rt and flush, so the GPU clocks settle before timing), reads tri as `s3d::instance_triangles(forest)`, then two times: start the clock, 20 times render to rt and flush, read the pixels of rt once, and keep the best time divided by 20. Run meshes first (save "i4_mesh"), then impostors (save "i4_imp"). Pass when the impostor triangles are at most 0.15 times the mesh triangles and the impostor frame time is at most 0.5 times the mesh one. Print "I4 cost: tris TI / TM frame FI / FM ms" (milliseconds) with " ok" or " FAIL". Set the forest's `visible` false and the ground `visible` false.
I5: set one `visible` true. th is 17 degrees in radians. For s from 0 to 44, d is 40 plus 0.5 times s; `aim((d times sine of th, 5, d times cosine of th), center, (0, 1, 0))`; r0 from `shot_none()`, rm from `shot_mesh()`, then set `visible` true, `imp` imp, `imp_distance` 50 and `imp_band` 14 and take ri from `shot(rt)` (save "i5_band" when s is 34). Masks against r0; the step passes when the count ratio is within 0.85 and 1.15 and the luminance error over the union is at most 0.12. Track the lowest and highest ratio and the largest luminance error; print "I5 hand-over: count LO..HI luma L" with " ok" or " FAIL".
Last print "impostor: ok" when all five pass, else "impostor: FAILED".
